":"Pure value patch → computed property","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Add"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition\/interpolate"},{"type":"text","text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property (or an inline expression) — no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", no side effect."}]},{"anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State","type":"heading","text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: ","type":"text"},{"code":"down","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"onTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onDoubleTap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"onLongPress","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose output lands in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or fires a callback. The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" helper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gesture arbitration clean.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic","type":"heading","text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sample and Hold","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, a ","type":"text"},{"code":".onChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or an assignment inside a ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block)."}]},{"anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation","type":"heading","text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"text":", and other animation patches drive a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"text":" modifier on the animated property.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Flag-dont-fake","type":"heading","text":"Flag, don’t fake","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absolute-position layout."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Beats":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four-beat discipline that keeps the translator honest: one pattern per branch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compile-clean before opening a PR, visual gate against Origami’s own render, ship"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only on Reviewer approval plus a human spot-check."}],"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Beats","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/beats"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction"}],"title":"Interaction","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" patch."}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/drag","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Drag"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" patch ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drag","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Drag","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Drag"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swami","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","title":"Swami"}}}